      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Neumann's Bar, opened in 1887, remains North St. Paul's oldest continuously operating bar, still serving drinks in its historic downtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_St._Paul%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "St Mark's Lutheran Church, founded in 1887, stands as one of North St. Paul's earliest religious institutions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_St._Paul%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Catholic Church of St. Peter, with its parochial school on Margaret Street, sits just north of North St. Paul's historic downtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_St._Paul%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The cornerstone of North St. Paul's church was laid in September 1915, and by 1916 the community added stained‑glass windows, pews, a pipe organ, and Italian marble altars.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_St._Paul%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Silver Lake and Casey Lake, North St. Paul's largest bodies of water, each boast large adjacent parks for outdoor recreation.",
